--------------------

Model of substitution: GTR+F+G4

Rate parameter R:

  A-C: 0.5828
  A-G: 2.8953
  A-T: 1.4862
  C-G: 0.7188
  C-T: 9.2464
  G-T: 1.0000

State frequencies: (empirical counts from alignment)

  pi(A) = 0.3226
  pi(C) = 0.1067
  pi(G) = 0.1376
  pi(T) = 0.4331

Rate matrix Q:

  A   -0.6467   0.03642    0.2333     0.377
  C    0.1101    -2.513   0.05791     2.345
  G    0.5471   0.04492   -0.8457    0.2537
  T    0.2808    0.5779   0.08057   -0.9393

Model of rate heterogeneity: Gamma with 4 categories
Gamma shape alpha: 0.368

 Category  Relative_rate  Proportion
  1         0.01238        0.25
  2         0.1575         0.25
  3         0.6942         0.25
  4         3.136          0.25
Relative rates are computed as MEAN of the portion of the Gamma distribution falling in the category.

